Z||000000||RZURCTN||01-07-2000||07:55 PM||||Here's the deal.  It's an 84 4cyl.  When the EGR valve is plugged into the vacuum line, the car runs really bad!  If I unplug it an cap off the vacuum line it runs fine.  At idle with the EGR plugged in it runs fine.  When I raise the rpm's and it gets a little vacuum, it starts to sputter, choke, fart, cough and wants to die.  Once the rpm's are raised and this condition starts, it persists, even at idle, until I disconnect the vacuum line again.  I checked the EGR valve out and even cleaned it.  It holds a vacuum without bleeding off.  Could it still be a bad valve or am I missing something else here?  Thanks in advance for the help!||||reg||8
Z||000001||88formula||01-07-2000||10:20 PM||||The EGR is definitely sticking open, replace the EGR valve and hook it back up. If you run your engine without it, you run the risk of damaging the engine through detonation. You could burn the pistons.||||reg||1
